# sf-audit Domain Weights Configuration
#
# Copy this file to sf-audit-weights-config.md and edit the values.
# The file is detected automatically by /sf-audit at runtime.
# It is excluded from git so your settings stay local.
#
# Rules:
# - All weights must be positive numbers
# - Weights do NOT need to sum to 100 — they are normalised automatically
# - Remove or comment out any domain to use its default weight
# - Set a domain weight to 0 to exclude it from scoring entirely

## Domain Weights

| Domain          | Default Weight | Your Weight |
|:----------------|:--------------:|:-----------:|
| security        |      20        |     20      |
| data            |      15        |     15      |
| automation      |      15        |     15      |
| architecture    |      12        |     12      |
| coverage        |       8        |      8      |
| naming          |       8        |      8      |
| orphaned        |       8        |      8      |
| descriptions    |       7        |      7      |
| field-sprawl    |       7        |      7      |

## Example: Prioritise security and data for a regulated industry org
#
# | Domain          | Your Weight |
# |:----------------|:-----------:|
# | security        |     35      |
# | data            |     25      |
# | automation      |     15      |
# | architecture    |     10      |
# | coverage        |      5      |
# | naming          |      3      |
# | orphaned        |      3      |
# | descriptions    |      2      |
# | field-sprawl    |      2      |

## Example: Exclude domains you don't want scored
#
# Set weight to 0 to exclude a domain from the composite score:
# | descriptions    |      0      |   ← excluded
# | field-sprawl    |      0      |   ← excluded
